            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic repair of a rectal fistula due to a benign ovarian dermoid cyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>383-386</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5468/ogs.2017.60.4.383</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ovarian dermoid cysts are one of the most common benign neoplasms in women. Rectal fistula formation due to an ovarian dermoid cyst, particularly a benign dermoid cyst, is extremely rare. A 17-year-old girl with symptoms of lower abdominal pain, passage of sebaceous materials in the stool, and hematochezia was found to have an 11-cm dermoid cyst complicated with a rectal fistula formation. Laparoscopic repair of the rectal fistula was performed successfully with bilateral ovarian cystectomies. This case presents the rare formation of a fistula between a benign dermoid cyst and the rectum and its treatment using laparoscopic repair without laparotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
